2026-07-27T15:21:52.5009952Z [36;1m# standard flags R selects per version (e.g. -std=gnu2x for C, -std=gnu++17[0m
2026-07-27T15:21:52.5010449Z [36;1m# / -std=gnu++20 for C++); a plain "CC = ccache gcc" override would drop[0m
2026-07-27T15:21:52.5010915Z [36;1m# them and silently downgrade the standard across the version matrix.[0m
2026-07-27T15:21:52.5011391Z [36;1m# Inference uses an empty user Makevars so we always read the pristine[0m
2026-07-27T15:21:52.5011832Z [36;1m# Makeconf defaults, never a value we just wrote.[0m
2026-07-27T15:21:52.5012249Z [36;1m# Note: the versioned switches (CXX11..CXX23) intentionally come out as[0m
2026-07-27T15:21:52.5012710Z [36;1m# bare "g++" with no -std flag. R keeps the standard in a separate[0m
